AI Control is a native macOS app that removes repeated setup work when using
Claude Code across many projects: coding principles, `.md` files, folder
structures, secrets, and update tracking. See `PROJECT.md` for the full spec
and `idea.md` for the original brief.

This repo's own `CLAUDE.md` is hand-authored, not generated by the global
module-merge system described in `PROJECT.md` §6.2 — that system doesn't
exist yet (this is the project building it), so `claude_md_generated` stays
`null` until AI Control can manage itself.

How to use: this project's own updates live in `updates/`, per its own
`CLAUDE.md` conventions.

Status: bootstrapping. Phase 0 (repo + tracking), Phase 1 (core
Project/Organizer scanning model), and Phase 2 (dashboard UI) done. Next up
is Phase 3 (project sidebar). See
`updates/2026-09-20 INIT - OPEN/update v1.md` for the full roadmap and status.
